================================================================================
Settings UI: Default button restores factory branding
================================================================================

Context
-------
Settings → Configuration → UI already previewed factory title, color, and logo
via a long "Reset to defaults" action. The control is now labeled Default, and
it also restores the factory default entity icon immediately.

Changes
-------
1. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Relabeled `#uiBrandingResetDefaultsBtn` to Default with an accessible
   restore-factory description.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   `resetUIBrandingDefaults()` still previews OntoBricks / #4F46E5 / bundled
   logo; it now also persists the factory entity icon (📦) when needed.
3. tests/units/front/test_ui_branding_settings_contract.py
   Contract coverage for the Default label and entity-icon reset.
4. documentation/user-guide.md
   Documented Default vs Save persistence for branding vs entity icon.
5. .cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc
   Runtime theme contract now names the Default button.

