================================================================================
Document UI branding persistence in user guide and Sphinx
================================================================================

Context
-------
Settings → Configuration → UI already persisted title/color/logo and the
default entity icon in registry `global_config`, but the user guide, API
guide, architecture notes, and Sphinx autodoc did not describe that path
or the Default button vs Save split.

Changes
-------
1. documentation/user-guide.md
   Added Default entity icon, registry persistence table, and Save vs
   Default write timing.
2. documentation/features.md
   Added a Navigation & UX bullet for configurable UI branding.
3. documentation/architecture.md
   Documented `ui_branding` on `GlobalConfigService` and the Lakebase
   `global_config` JSONB payload.
4. documentation/api.md
   Documented `GET`/`POST /settings/ui-branding`.
5. README.md
   Clarified that branding lives in registry `global_config`.
6. documentation/sphinx/api/app.core.helpers.rst
   Autodoc for `back.core.helpers.UIBranding`.
7. documentation/sphinx/api/app.fastapi.rst
   Autodoc for `shared.fastapi.ui_branding`.
8. `ci/build_docs.sh`
   Rebuilt Sphinx HTML (no new warnings for the branding modules).

